{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-markdown-remark-js","path":"/community-handbook/elyra/docs/source/setup-initial-environment.md","result":{"data":{"site":{"siteMetadata":{"title":"Operate First"}},"markdownRemark":{"id":"80d1e304-c2cd-58ab-958a-2b3851cc4d17","html":"<h1 id=\"setup-initial-environment\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#setup-initial-environment\" aria-label=\"setup initial environment permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>Setup initial environment</h1>\n<p>In this tutorial we rely on a <a href=\"https://github.com/aicoe-aiops/project-template\">project template</a> in order to have a common structure that can be easily used by data scientists and devops engineers. Having structure in a project ensures all the pieces required for the ML and DevOps lifecycles are present and easily discoverable.</p>\n<p>If you want to use this template for your AI project, go to the project template <a href=\"https://github.com/aicoe-aiops/project-template\">here</a> and click the <code class=\"language-text\">Use the template</code> button provided in the repository.</p>\n<div style=\"text-align:center\">\n<img alt=\"AI Project Template\" src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thoth-station/elyra-aidevsecops-tutorial/master/docs/images/AIProjectTemplate.png\">\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"1-fork-this-repo-from-github-into-your-account\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#1-fork-this-repo-from-github-into-your-account\" aria-label=\"1 fork this repo from github into your account permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>1. Fork this repo from GitHub into your account</h2>\n<p>To begin, you’ll need to fork this repository to create your own copy. If you’re unsure how, look at <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/github/getting-started-with-github/fork-a-repo\">Fork a Repo</a> from GitHub docs.</p>\n<h2 id=\"2-access-the-elyra-image-in-jupyterhub\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#2-access-the-elyra-image-in-jupyterhub\" aria-label=\"2 access the elyra image in jupyterhub permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>2. Access the Elyra image in JupyterHub</h2>\n<h3 id=\"access-jupyterhub-set-up-by-project-meteor\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#access-jupyterhub-set-up-by-project-meteor\" aria-label=\"access jupyterhub set up by project meteor permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>Access JupyterHub set up by Project Meteor</h3>\n<p>If you are viewing this tutorial in the Jupyter Book rendered by <a href=\"https://github.com/AICoE/meteor\">Project Meteor</a>, you can simply hover over the rocket icon on the top right of the page, and click on the <code class=\"language-text\">JupyterHub</code> option. This will take you to a JupyterLab environment spawned with the Elyra AIDevSecOps Tutorial image. Alternatively, you can also access this environment by clicking the <code class=\"language-text\">JupyterHub</code> button on the spawning page of the Meteor web application.\nMoreover, using Meteor, the URL of your GitHub repo already add your repo to <a href=\"https://github.com/jupyterlab/jupyterlab-git\">JupyterLab Git</a> extension. Therefore that repo is already synced and managed by the extension.</p>\n<h3 id=\"access-jupyterhub-set-up-by-operate-first\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#access-jupyterhub-set-up-by-operate-first\" aria-label=\"access jupyterhub set up by operate first permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>Access JupyterHub set up by Operate First</h3>\n<p>If you’re viewing this tutorial outside of the Jupyter Book rendered by Project Meteor, you can instead access the <a href=\"https://jupyter.org/hub\">JupyterHub</a> deployed on the <a href=\"https://www.operate-first.cloud/\">Operate First</a> cluster.</p>\n<ol class=\"pf-c-list\">\n<li>\n<p>Click this <a href=\"https://jupyterhub-opf-jupyterhub.apps.smaug.na.operate-first.cloud/\">link</a> to visit the Operate First JupyterHub.</p>\n<div style=\"text-align:center\">\n<img alt=\"Jupyter Hub UI\" src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thoth-station/elyra-aidevsecops-tutorial/master/docs/images/JupyterHubNewUI.png\">\n</div>\n</li>\n<li>Select the image called <code class=\"language-text\">AICoE Elyra AIDevSecOps Tutorial Notebook Image</code>.</li>\n<li>Select <code class=\"language-text\">Large</code> for container size.</li>\n<li>\n<p>Insert the environment variables required using the add button in JupyterLab UI:</p>\n<ul class=\"pf-c-list\">\n<li><code class=\"language-text\">AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"language-text\">AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"language-text\">OBJECT_STORAGE_ENDPOINT_URL</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"language-text\">OBJECT_STORAGE_BUCKET_NAME</code></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"3-clone-your-repo-using-jupyterlab-git-extension\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#3-clone-your-repo-using-jupyterlab-git-extension\" aria-label=\"3 clone your repo using jupyterlab git extension permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>3. Clone your repo using Jupyterlab Git Extension</h2>\n<p>Once your image is ready and you are in the Jupyterlab UI, you can use the Git extension provided to clone this repo.</p>\n<ol class=\"pf-c-list\">\n<li>\n<p>Click the Git extension button from Jupyterlab UI:</p>\n<div style=\"text-align:center\">\n<img alt=\"Look for Git extension button\" src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thoth-station/elyra-aidevsecops-tutorial/master/docs/images/ElyraGitExtension.png\">\n</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Take HTTPS link of the GitHub repo you want to clone, for this tutorial use your forked one from this repo:</p>\n<div style=\"text-align:center\">\n<img alt=\"Take link from forked repo\" src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thoth-station/elyra-aidevsecops-tutorial/master/docs/images/TakeLinkForkedRepo.png\">\n</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Insert the link taken from your forked repo in the JupyterLab Git Extension: e.g. <code class=\"language-text\">https://github.com/thoth-station/elyra-aidevsecops-tutorial.git</code></p>\n<div style=\"text-align:center\">\n<img alt=\"Clone your repo\" src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thoth-station/elyra-aidevsecops-tutorial/master/docs/images/CloneYourRepo.png\">\n</div>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"next-step\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#next-step\" aria-label=\"next step permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>Next Step</h2>\n<p><a href=\"./explore-notebooks-and-manage-dependencies.md\">Explore notebooks and manage dependencies</a></p>\n<h2 id=\"references\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#references\" aria-label=\"references permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>References</h2>\n<ul class=\"pf-c-list\">\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/aicoe-aiops/project-template\">Project template</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/AICoE/meteor\">Project Meteor</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://jupyter.org/hub\">JupyterHub</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.operate-first.cloud/\">Operate First</a></li>\n</ul>","fields":{"srcLink":"https://github.com/thoth-station/elyra-aidevsecops-tutorial/blob/master/docs/source/setup-initial-environment.md"},"frontmatter":{"title":"","description":null,"extraClasses":null,"banner":null}}},"pageContext":{"id":"80d1e304-c2cd-58ab-958a-2b3851cc4d17"}},"staticQueryHashes":["1764348645","2823140819","3000541721","3606484676"]}